<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Fed is expected to add reserves to the banking system via overnight system repurchase agreements Tuesday, analysts said.</p>
<p>Fed funds remained tight today at 5-13/16 percent after trading well above 6.0 percent Monday.</p>
<p>High Treasury balances at the Fed was said keeping pressure on funds.</p>
<p>Monday, the Fed added reserves through overnight system RPs, totalling $8.65 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
